  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** AMC Robotics is shifting its AI-driven robotics platforms from development to early commercialization. NovaArm™ entered a live warehouse trial through a collaboration with Sunward Logistics, while Kyro™ attracted attention at CES. The company serves the U.S., Canada, and Europe. Demand remains unproven, and negligible historical revenue visibility plus extreme share volatility reflect deep market skepticism. The competitive robotics landscape adds pressure, making meaningful adoption uncertain for now.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Under CEO Sean Da, management is pivoting toward initial deployments, evidenced by the NovaArm pilot and a first quarterly net profit. However, this progress is overshadowed by heavy past shareholder dilution and a cash runway of less than a year. Analyst sentiment is predominantly bearish with sell ratings, though one upgrade to hold hints at stabilization. Converting early interest into sustainable, scalable contracts is critical to restoring credibility and securing the company’s future.",
